# The release artifact is the component itself. `git archive` honours these, so
# the release tooling — and this file — never rides along into a user's machine.
# `.gitignore`/`pyproject.toml`/`tests/` stay: the artifact is then the same set
# of files a dev checkout tar carries (host's scripts/build-component-tar.sh).
#
# The leading slashes are load-bearing. An unanchored `scripts/` is a pattern
# matched at EVERY depth, so it also dropped `skills/readme-crafter/scripts/` —
# the scanner the skill's SKILL.md tells the agent to run — from every release,
# while a dev checkout kept it: the skill shipped broken and nothing here said
# so, because the suite runs against the checkout.
/.github/ export-ignore
/scripts/ export-ignore
/.gitattributes export-ignore
